1
00:00:10,844 --> 00:00:15,390
<i>We will now begin</i>
<i>the first prison match, Heavy 13.</i>

2
00:00:15,473 --> 00:00:18,518
<i>As Hong Jin-ho</i>
<i>had the highest ranking in the main match,</i>

3
00:00:18,601 --> 00:00:20,687
<i>the first-player marker will go to him.</i>

4
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:23,732
Round 1 will now begin.

5
00:00:23,815 --> 00:00:27,110
Please set down a rock card
and a color chip facing down.

6
00:00:39,664 --> 00:00:41,332
Everyone is stepping back.

7
00:00:41,416 --> 00:00:42,792
It just feels like we should.

8
00:00:47,797 --> 00:00:49,507
Don't set down your red chip.

9
00:00:49,591 --> 00:00:50,717
Huh?

10
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:51,926
Mind games, huh?

11
00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:53,428
- Look at you.
- Isn't that how it's done?

12
00:00:54,095 --> 00:00:55,430
I was gonna go for that.

13
00:00:56,222 --> 00:00:59,893
Going in, I thought I needed to
use up the six

14
00:00:59,976 --> 00:01:02,771
<i>to deal with the high-numbered rock card</i>
<i>as soon as possible.</i>

15
00:01:02,854 --> 00:01:05,440
<i>My strategy was to get rid of</i>
<i>the higher cards first.</i>

16
00:01:05,523 --> 00:01:09,069
Later on, if I have to play high
while the others play low,

17
00:01:09,152 --> 00:01:11,071
this might give me
a positional advantage.

18
00:01:11,154 --> 00:01:14,449
But once rainbow chips
and other mechanics enter,

19
00:01:14,532 --> 00:01:16,451
I'd be a sitting duck.

20
00:01:16,534 --> 00:01:20,497
<i>So I wanted to save my lower cards</i>
<i>to avoid penalty points later.</i>

21
00:01:24,375 --> 00:01:25,418
Should I go for a different color?

22
00:01:25,502 --> 00:01:26,878
Yeah, don't use the green chip.

23
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:32,926
Submissions are now closed.
Please reveal your color chip.

24
00:01:34,844 --> 00:01:36,846
Red, the color of passion.

25
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:38,473
Oh man, three red chips.

26
00:01:38,556 --> 00:01:40,058
Thank goodness.

27
00:01:40,141 --> 00:01:41,351
Three red chips.

28
00:01:42,143 --> 00:01:43,853
Please reveal your rock card.

29
00:01:43,937 --> 00:01:44,938
Two, two, three.

30
00:01:46,564 --> 00:01:47,482
Six, right?

31
00:01:49,234 --> 00:01:50,777
This is exactly
what I was worried about.

32
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:52,570
Oh man.

33
00:01:53,196 --> 00:01:54,864
- What now?
- Guess we all had the same idea.

34
00:01:54,948 --> 00:01:56,908
So we're all on the same level.

35
00:01:56,991 --> 00:01:58,451
They all had the same idea.

36
00:01:58,535 --> 00:02:00,787
Six is better. You get to go first.

37
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:02,163
- JAE JAE.
- Yes?

38
00:02:02,247 --> 00:02:03,915
- Would you like to place?
- I'm up first?

39
00:02:03,998 --> 00:02:06,709
<i>With no rainbow chip in play,</i>

40
00:02:06,793 --> 00:02:09,129
<i>the player who submitted card six</i>
<i>will go first,</i>

41
00:02:09,212 --> 00:02:11,047
<i>as it is the highest number in this round.</i>

42
00:02:11,131 --> 00:02:12,757
<i>If the numbers are tied,</i>

43
00:02:12,841 --> 00:02:16,970
<i>the player closest to the first player</i>
<i>in a clockwise order goes first.</i>

44
00:02:17,053 --> 00:02:18,638
JAE JAE, would you like to place?

45
00:02:18,721 --> 00:02:20,473
Yes, I'd like to place.

46
00:02:20,557 --> 00:02:23,059
- You have placed six on green.
- Okay.

47
00:02:23,643 --> 00:02:26,146
- Jeong Hyun-gyu, would you like to place?
- Yes.

48
00:02:26,229 --> 00:02:28,523
You have placed six on red.

49
00:02:28,606 --> 00:02:32,068
- Hong Jin-ho, would you like to place?
- Jin-ho, pass. Let's all have some fun.

50
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:34,946
I'm not gonna pass.

51
00:02:35,029 --> 00:02:35,864
I'd like to place.

52
00:02:35,947 --> 00:02:38,074
You have placed five on red.

53
00:02:39,701 --> 00:02:41,703
- Stella Jang, would you like to place?
- Yes.

54
00:02:41,786 --> 00:02:44,080
- John Park, would you like to place?
- Yes.

55
00:02:44,164 --> 00:02:46,666
