80
00:03:41,304 --> 00:03:43,264
Do they all see 7high
as their rival or something?

81
00:03:46,976 --> 00:03:48,436
Look at him, trying to get a cool shot.

82
00:03:48,519 --> 00:03:49,979
- So cool.
- Nice.

83
00:03:50,063 --> 00:03:51,272
The 7high act.

84
00:03:51,356 --> 00:03:52,315
XITSUH…

85
00:03:55,235 --> 00:03:56,319
Is he a goner?

86
00:03:57,320 --> 00:04:00,365
Submissions are now closed.
Please reveal your color chip.

87
00:04:00,448 --> 00:04:01,407
Any rainbow?

88
00:04:02,408 --> 00:04:04,202
Man, this is tough.

89
00:04:05,495 --> 00:04:07,080
We might be thinking the same thing.

90
00:04:07,163 --> 00:04:08,331
There you go!

91
00:04:08,873 --> 00:04:10,333
I knew I could count on XITSUH.

92
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,252
Me?

93
00:04:12,335 --> 00:04:14,003
I've been counting on you, XITSUH.

94
00:04:14,087 --> 00:04:15,838
Oh, I'll be fine. Thank goodness.

95
00:04:18,591 --> 00:04:20,510
XITSUH, would you like to place?

96
00:04:20,593 --> 00:04:23,221
- Yes.
- You have placed six on red.

97
00:04:23,304 --> 00:04:24,430
I'll go for it.

98
00:04:24,514 --> 00:04:25,765
You have placed three on blue.

99
00:04:27,558 --> 00:04:29,143
You have received two penalty points.

100
00:04:29,727 --> 00:04:32,272
He avoided using a pass
to get one less penalty point.

101
00:04:32,355 --> 00:04:36,150
He only got two penalty points
as opposed to three.

102
00:04:36,234 --> 00:04:38,361
I can't believe you went with two.

103
00:04:38,444 --> 00:04:39,904
He always goes for two.

104
00:04:39,988 --> 00:04:41,030
It's Round 2, after all.

105
00:04:41,114 --> 00:04:42,907
- Ha Seok-jin, would you like to place?
- Yes.

106
00:04:42,991 --> 00:04:44,701
You have placed three on green.

107
00:04:44,784 --> 00:04:46,786
Man, trying your luck with one?

108
00:04:46,869 --> 00:04:48,204
You have received two penalty points.

109
00:04:50,164 --> 00:04:52,458
Hong Jin-ho, you have placed two on blue.

110
00:04:52,542 --> 00:04:54,043
John Park, would you like to place?

111
00:04:54,127 --> 00:04:56,421
- Yes.
- You have placed two on red.

112
00:04:58,381 --> 00:05:00,258
You have received two penalty points.

113
00:05:00,341 --> 00:05:01,426
What a narrow escape.

114
00:05:04,345 --> 00:05:06,431
- JAE JAE, would you like to place?
- Yes, please.

115
00:05:06,514 --> 00:05:08,016
You have placed one on red.

116
00:05:08,099 --> 00:05:10,935
- Stella Jang, you have placed on green.
- Yes.

117
00:05:11,019 --> 00:05:12,770
That concludes Round 2.

118
00:05:12,854 --> 00:05:15,315
The first-player marker
will go to John Park.

119
00:05:15,815 --> 00:05:17,317
Round 3 will now begin.

120
00:05:19,610 --> 00:05:21,154
Which combo?

121
00:05:29,829 --> 00:05:30,997
<i>Six can be useful</i>

122
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:34,584
<i>when other players have just received</i>
<i>penalty points in the previous round.</i>

123
00:05:34,667 --> 00:05:37,962
You can come on strong and go first.

124
00:05:38,046 --> 00:05:41,758
<i>I realized that you might not have to</i>
<i>discard six right away.</i>

125
00:05:41,841 --> 00:05:44,510
- This would be a good time to play six.
- If you still have it?

126
00:05:44,594 --> 00:05:47,680
Playing high numbers up front
isn't always better.

127
00:05:47,764 --> 00:05:48,973
This is fun.

128
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:52,226
Submissions are now closed.

129
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:53,728
Please reveal your color chip.

130
00:05:56,147 --> 00:05:57,523
A rainbow.

131
00:05:58,232 --> 00:05:59,609
John and I keep overlapping.

132
00:06:01,152 --> 00:06:03,071
- What a mess.
- This isn't good.

133
00:06:03,654 --> 00:06:06,407
