248
00:10:42,266 --> 00:10:44,352
John Park, would you like to place?

249
00:10:44,435 --> 00:10:46,270
- Yes.
- You have placed one on green.

250
00:10:46,354 --> 00:10:47,980
You have received five penalty points.

251
00:10:48,064 --> 00:10:50,775
If he used his zero
and it collapsed on him…

252
00:10:50,858 --> 00:10:52,026
- Then that'd be six points.
- Yeah.

253
00:10:52,109 --> 00:10:53,444
- It's better to take the hit now.
- Yeah.

254
00:10:54,028 --> 00:10:56,364
JAE JAE and XITSUH, you have placed.

255
00:10:57,031 --> 00:10:58,282
That concludes Round 5.

256
00:10:58,366 --> 00:10:59,784
We're just getting started.

257
00:10:59,867 --> 00:11:00,868
This is where it gets serious.

258
00:11:00,951 --> 00:11:02,244
- It's all about what remains.
- Right.

259
00:11:02,328 --> 00:11:04,455
Many will still have their zeros
and rainbows.

260
00:11:04,538 --> 00:11:06,040
Round 6 will now begin.

261
00:11:06,123 --> 00:11:08,959
Please set down a rock card
and a color chip facing down.

262
00:11:18,886 --> 00:11:20,262
Submissions are now closed.

263
00:11:20,346 --> 00:11:21,764
Please reveal your color chip.

264
00:11:21,847 --> 00:11:22,848
It's all rainbows, no?

265
00:11:23,766 --> 00:11:25,434
Plenty have used
their rainbow chips already.

266
00:11:25,518 --> 00:11:27,061
It's a sea of blue.

267
00:11:27,144 --> 00:11:28,437
Please reveal your rock card.

268
00:11:30,147 --> 00:11:32,149
Damn it. I think I'm screwed.

269
00:11:33,275 --> 00:11:35,236
Wow. You still had your six?

270
00:11:35,319 --> 00:11:36,862
That's amazing.

271
00:11:36,946 --> 00:11:38,656
- JAE JAE, would you like to place?
- Yes.

272
00:11:38,739 --> 00:11:40,783
Where should I place it?

273
00:11:41,784 --> 00:11:45,329
If you go with blue,
Stella will get the penalty points.

274
00:11:45,413 --> 00:11:48,332
If you go with red, John will get them.

275
00:11:48,416 --> 00:11:51,001
This is too dangerous.
Blue won't collapse, right?

276
00:11:51,085 --> 00:11:52,795
- There's still the next round.
- Right.

277
00:11:52,878 --> 00:11:58,592
<i>In the next round, JAE JAE has no choice</i>
<i>but to play her blue chip and card two.</i>

278
00:11:58,676 --> 00:12:03,180
<i>If she doesn't place her rock cube</i>
<i>on the blue stand in this round,</i>

279
00:12:03,264 --> 00:12:07,643
<i>it will carry over into Round 7</i>
<i>fully loaded.</i>

280
00:12:07,727 --> 00:12:10,521
<i>Since she only has a blue chip remaining,</i>

281
00:12:10,604 --> 00:12:12,773
<i>this would spell disaster for her.</i>

282
00:12:12,857 --> 00:12:15,192
Blue. I have to avoid it
collapsing on me later.

283
00:12:15,276 --> 00:12:16,444
- Shoot, sorry.
- JAE JAE.

284
00:12:16,527 --> 00:12:18,070
- So how many for me?
- You have placed three on blue.

285
00:12:18,738 --> 00:12:21,407
Team play in this game
is surprisingly difficult.

286
00:12:21,490 --> 00:12:23,242
The situation keeps changing.

287
00:12:23,951 --> 00:12:26,036
Hong Jin-ho, would you like to place?

288
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:28,539
- Yes, please.
- You have placed six on blue.

289
00:12:28,622 --> 00:12:30,958
John Park, you have placed four on red.

290
00:12:31,041 --> 00:12:33,419
Stella Jang, would you like to place?

291
00:12:35,296 --> 00:12:37,840
- Yes.
- You have placed two on blue.

292
00:12:39,091 --> 00:12:41,427
- You have received three penalty points.
- We're tied now.

293
00:12:41,510 --> 00:12:43,220
You're fine.

294
00:12:43,304 --> 00:12:45,181
- It's not a critical hit.
- At least the two zeros

295
00:12:45,264 --> 00:12:46,849
- aren't on the stand yet.
- Right.

296
00:12:46,932 --> 00:12:48,184
- Could've been worse.
- Yeah.

297
00:12:48,267 --> 00:12:50,728
XITSUH, you have placed one on green.

298
00:12:51,604 --> 00:12:53,022
Green is becoming really dangerous.

299
00:12:53,105 --> 00:12:54,231
It really is.

300
00:12:54,857 --> 00:12:56,776
Jeong Hyun-gyu,
you have placed zero on blue.

301
00:12:56,859 --> 00:12:59,278
Ha Seok-jin, you have placed zero on blue.

302
00:12:59,361 --> 00:13:00,654
All the stands are about to blow.

303
00:13:00,738 --> 00:13:02,198
That concludes Round 6.

304
00:13:02,281 --> 00:13:04,825
As Stella Jang was the last
to receive penalty points,

305
00:13:04,909 --> 00:13:06,577
the first-player marker will go to her.

306
00:13:06,660 --> 00:13:09,789
- Only low cards remain, right?
- No big numbers left now.

307
00:13:09,872 --> 00:13:10,706
Right.

308
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:12,249
This is so scary.

309
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:13,793
- Oh man.
- The zeros will start piling up.

310
00:13:13,876 --> 00:13:17,505
Guys with more than five penalty points
must be getting nervous.

311
00:13:17,588 --> 00:13:18,547
Of course.

312
00:13:19,131 --> 00:13:20,716
Round 7 will now begin.

313
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:22,676
Please reveal your color chip.

314
00:13:23,969 --> 00:13:25,054
Only one green?

315
00:13:26,055 --> 00:13:27,598
- I'm jealous.
- Please reveal your rock card.

316
00:13:27,681 --> 00:13:28,682
There are rainbows.

317
00:13:33,729 --> 00:13:35,105
It'll really pile on now.

318
00:13:35,189 --> 00:13:37,650
- I can't even target anyone right now.
- No, you can't.

319
00:13:37,733 --> 00:13:39,151
- You'll have to let it carry over.
- Yeah.

320
00:13:39,235 --> 00:13:40,361
That's a mighty bomb.

321
00:13:40,861 --> 00:13:42,196
What should we do, Seok-jin?

322
00:13:44,949 --> 00:13:47,326
Since we're in the upper ranks,

323
00:13:47,409 --> 00:13:49,078
it'd make more sense to spread it out.

324
00:13:49,787 --> 00:13:51,205
We shouldn't bite off too much.

325
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:55,084
- Blue is no joke.
- Either way…

326
00:13:55,167 --> 00:13:56,710
- I'll just go for blue.
- Jeong Hyun-gyu.

327
00:13:56,794 --> 00:13:58,587
You have placed one on blue.

328
00:13:59,588 --> 00:14:00,756
I'll go for green.

329
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:02,675
You have placed one on green.

330
00:14:02,758 --> 00:14:04,969
JAE JAE, you have placed two on blue.

331
00:14:05,052 --> 00:14:07,680
Stella Jang, you have placed zero on red.

332
00:14:07,763 --> 00:14:10,099
John Park, you have placed zero on blue.

333
00:14:10,182 --> 00:14:12,101
XITSUH, you have placed zero on blue.

334
00:14:12,184 --> 00:14:13,561
Blue is getting insane.

335
00:14:13,644 --> 00:14:15,771
Hong Jin-ho,
you have placed zero on green.

336
00:14:15,855 --> 00:14:18,065
- We're in trouble.
- That concludes Round 7.

337
00:14:18,148 --> 00:14:19,358
Just as I thought.

338
00:14:19,441 --> 00:14:21,485
If someone adds a six there…

339
00:14:21,569 --> 00:14:22,778
That's hell.

340
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:25,781
This game can send you packing in one go.

341
00:14:25,865 --> 00:14:28,701
That could collapse on us too.

342
00:14:28,784 --> 00:14:31,662
We will now distribute
a fresh set of rock cards and color chips.

343
00:14:33,706 --> 00:14:35,749
Do I have to start with a rainbow?

344
00:14:37,042 --> 00:14:38,419
I can't take all those penalty points.

345
00:14:38,502 --> 00:14:39,879
Round 8 will now begin.

346
00:14:40,379 --> 00:14:43,382
Please set down a rock card
and a color chip facing down.

347
00:14:58,564 --> 00:14:59,565
Stella.

348
00:14:59,648 --> 00:15:02,860
Do you have a color in mind?

349
00:15:02,943 --> 00:15:06,405
I'm thinking blue with a high number.

350
00:15:06,906 --> 00:15:10,659
- I doubt people would use a rainbow now.
- I'll choose green, then.

351
00:15:12,536 --> 00:15:14,204
I went for zero on red.

352
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:15,956
Zero.

353
00:15:17,458 --> 00:15:18,459
John.

354
00:15:18,542 --> 00:15:20,002
A high number?

355
00:15:20,085 --> 00:15:21,503
- Yeah, I think so.
- One minute left.

356
00:15:25,507 --> 00:15:27,051
Damn it. I'm not sure.

357
00:15:28,302 --> 00:15:30,012
- Submissions are now closed.
- I don't know anymore.

358
00:15:30,095 --> 00:15:31,680
Please reveal your color chip.

359
00:15:32,222 --> 00:15:34,141
- Please.
- Did anyone play a rainbow from the start?

360
00:15:35,142 --> 00:15:36,727
Do we have such gutsy… Wait, what?

361
00:15:43,025 --> 00:15:44,068
Damn it.

362
00:15:45,402 --> 00:15:46,862
A whopping two?

363
00:15:47,529 --> 00:15:49,907
- I'm screwed.
- Please reveal your rock card.

364
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:52,785
I'm safe.

365
00:15:59,667 --> 00:16:02,461
I'm in danger.

366
00:16:02,544 --> 00:16:05,297
- Jeong Hyun-gyu.
- Six on blue.

367
00:16:05,381 --> 00:16:07,132
You have placed six on blue.

368
00:16:08,175 --> 00:16:09,760
That's coming to me.

369
00:16:10,511 --> 00:16:12,763
- XITSUH.
- Six on green.

370
00:16:12,846 --> 00:16:14,723
You have placed six on green.

371
00:16:16,809 --> 00:16:18,811
Stella Jang, would you like to place?

372
00:16:22,022 --> 00:16:23,148
I'll take the penalty points.

373
00:16:23,232 --> 00:16:25,359
- Oh no.
- You have added six on blue.

374
00:16:25,442 --> 00:16:27,569
- You have received eight penalty points.
- Why'd you play a six?

375
00:16:27,653 --> 00:16:30,030
Goodness, poor Stella.

376
00:16:30,823 --> 00:16:32,449
She's a new elimination candidate.

377
00:16:32,533 --> 00:16:34,493
I'm going home. Damn it.

378
00:16:34,576 --> 00:16:35,619
Oh no.

379
00:16:38,205 --> 00:16:40,916
- John Park, would you like to place?
- Yes.

380
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,584
You have placed six on green.

381
00:16:42,668 --> 00:16:44,420
You have received seven penalty points.

382
00:16:45,629 --> 00:16:48,132
That was the worst possible choice.
In hindsight, but still.

383
00:16:53,679 --> 00:16:55,723
You never know what might happen.

384
00:16:55,806 --> 00:16:56,807
I think I do.

385
00:16:56,890 --> 00:16:58,225
You never know.

386
00:16:58,726 --> 00:17:00,894
- Ha Seok-jin, would you like to place?
- Yes.

387
00:17:00,978 --> 00:17:02,771
You have placed six on red.

388
00:17:03,439 --> 00:17:04,857
You have received four penalty points.

389
00:17:04,940 --> 00:17:06,150
It was bound to happen.

390
00:17:06,692 --> 00:17:08,277
That's not a bad call.

391
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:09,945
Yeah, because he only had
two penalty points.

392
00:17:10,029 --> 00:17:11,572
He can afford to take the hit.

393
00:17:11,655 --> 00:17:13,907
Hong Jin-ho, you have placed zero on blue.

394
00:17:13,991 --> 00:17:15,951
JAE JAE, you have placed zero on red.

395
00:17:16,035 --> 00:17:17,453
That concludes Round 8.

396
00:17:19,371 --> 00:17:21,206
Damn, -13 and -14.

397
00:17:21,707 --> 00:17:26,295
John and Stella
must be close to having a meltdown.

398
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:32,384
We need to stack a lot of lower numbers
and have one person take the hit.

399
00:17:32,468 --> 00:17:33,385
Yeah.

400
00:17:34,678 --> 00:17:35,971
Round 9 will now begin.

401
00:17:36,055 --> 00:17:38,974
Please set down a rock card
and a color chip facing down.

402
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:42,144
I'm screwed.

403
00:17:43,604 --> 00:17:44,521
No, that's not it.

404
00:17:45,147 --> 00:17:46,482
Hold on.

405
00:17:46,565 --> 00:17:47,733
No, it's right.

406
00:17:47,816 --> 00:17:49,068
Why wouldn't it be?

407
00:17:49,902 --> 00:17:51,945
I'm really not sure about this one.

408
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:54,239
I went for six on green.

409
00:17:59,036 --> 00:18:02,664
I'm sure the rest
are aiming for first place.

410
00:18:02,748 --> 00:18:04,083
Four Pieces for the winner, right?

411
00:18:04,166 --> 00:18:05,000
That's a lot.

412
00:18:05,084 --> 00:18:06,502
That's a lovely bonus.

413
00:18:06,585 --> 00:18:09,630
CURRENT 1ST PLACE: -2 POINTS

414
00:18:09,713 --> 00:18:12,257
CURRENT 2ND PLACE: -4 POINTS
CURRENT 3RD PLACE: -5 POINTS

415
00:18:12,341 --> 00:18:14,843
CURRENT 4TH PLACE: -6 POINTS
CURRENT 5TH PLACE: -7 POINTS

416
00:18:14,927 --> 00:18:19,515
But I don't think anyone
will come close to -13 or -14 points.

417
00:18:19,598 --> 00:18:20,724
You never know.

418
00:18:20,808 --> 00:18:21,642
CURRENT 7TH PLACE: -14 POINTS

419
00:18:21,725 --> 00:18:24,269
When the gap is that overwhelmingly large,

420
00:18:24,353 --> 00:18:26,146
- they're guaranteed to go down.
- Yeah.

421
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:28,440
- It's basically been decided now.
- Just let them go.

422
00:18:28,524 --> 00:18:30,275
All they need to do
is stay above those two,

423
00:18:30,359 --> 00:18:31,819
so it's fine to take some hits.

424
00:18:31,902 --> 00:18:34,071
John and Stella will likely be going home.

425
00:18:34,154 --> 00:18:35,572
Almost definitely.

426
00:18:35,656 --> 00:18:37,116
- Submissions are now closed.
- Okay.

427
00:18:37,199 --> 00:18:38,534
Please reveal your color chip.

428
00:18:41,995 --> 00:18:43,747
- Oh my gosh.
- Thank goodness.

429
00:18:43,831 --> 00:18:45,082
That's it for me.

430
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,418
Please reveal your rock card.

431
00:18:58,011 --> 00:19:01,348
Stella and John are feeling the pressure.

432
00:19:01,431 --> 00:19:03,100
They're playing their zeros and ones.

433
00:19:04,351 --> 00:19:05,310
That's really dangerous.

434
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:08,480
Hong Jin-ho, would you like to place?

435
00:19:08,564 --> 00:19:10,190
Yes, please.

436
00:19:10,274 --> 00:19:11,859
Please choose a color.

437
00:19:17,698 --> 00:19:20,951
<i>If I place my cube on red,</i>
<i>XITSUH would take the hit.</i>

438
00:19:21,034 --> 00:19:22,327
<i>If I place it on a different color,</i>

439
00:19:22,411 --> 00:19:24,538
<i>Hyun-gyu or someone else</i>
<i>might take the hit.</i>

440
00:19:25,581 --> 00:19:26,415
Shall I end you?

441
00:19:28,167 --> 00:19:29,126
Please spare me.

442
00:19:29,209 --> 00:19:31,295
- I say red. You can damage him too.
- Please spare me.

443
00:19:31,378 --> 00:19:33,505
- Green will collapse regardless.
- Right.

444
00:19:33,589 --> 00:19:35,716
<i>It was bothering me</i>
<i>that Hyun-gyu and Seok-jin</i>

445
00:19:35,799 --> 00:19:37,801
<i>were conferring with each other.</i>

446
00:19:37,885 --> 00:19:39,469
<i>Instead of letting these cliques sit,</i>

447
00:19:39,553 --> 00:19:41,889
<i>I decided to lend a hand</i>

448
00:19:41,972 --> 00:19:44,349
<i>and have XITSUH indebted to me</i>
<i>to win him over later.</i>

449
00:19:44,433 --> 00:19:45,809
- He would get--
- I'll go for green.

450
00:19:46,393 --> 00:19:48,061
You have placed two on green.

451
00:19:50,355 --> 00:19:52,232
He could've taken the hit.

452
00:19:52,316 --> 00:19:54,443
JAE JAE, would you like to place?

453
00:19:54,526 --> 00:19:55,777
I'll pass.

454
00:19:55,861 --> 00:19:57,863
XITSUH, would you like to place?

455
00:19:57,946 --> 00:19:58,906
Yes.

456
00:19:59,489 --> 00:20:00,699
You have placed five on red.

457
00:20:03,702 --> 00:20:05,579
- Ha Seok-jin.
- I'll place.

458
00:20:05,662 --> 00:20:07,915
- Jeong Hyun-gyu, would you like to place?
- Yes.

459
00:20:07,998 --> 00:20:10,459
Jeong Hyun-gyu,
you have placed three on green.

460
00:20:10,542 --> 00:20:11,877
You have received three penalty points.

461
00:20:12,461 --> 00:20:13,378
Cute.

462
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:14,880
Not a bad call.

463
00:20:15,714 --> 00:20:17,758
- John Park, would you like to place?
- Yes.

464
00:20:17,841 --> 00:20:19,509
You have placed one on blue.

465
00:20:19,593 --> 00:20:22,012
Stella Jang, you have placed zero on red.

466
00:20:22,095 --> 00:20:24,681
JAE JAE, you have placed six on green.

467
00:20:24,765 --> 00:20:26,225
That concludes Round 9.

468
00:20:26,308 --> 00:20:28,644
As Jeong Hyun-gyu was the last
to receive penalty points,

469
00:20:28,727 --> 00:20:30,354
the first-player marker will go to him.

470
00:20:30,437 --> 00:20:33,232
I'm relieved. I'm good as long as XITSUH
doesn't get eliminated.

471
00:20:33,315 --> 00:20:35,484
- He does seem safe.
- I want him to stay in the game.

472
00:20:35,567 --> 00:20:36,443
I saved you.

473
00:20:36,526 --> 00:20:37,903
I have an excellent memory.

474
00:20:37,986 --> 00:20:39,446
I'll forget tomorrow.

475
00:20:40,447 --> 00:20:41,823
Round 10 will now begin.

476
00:20:41,907 --> 00:20:45,285
Please set down a rock card
and a color chip facing down.

477
00:20:46,828 --> 00:20:49,498
Nothing is safe right now.

478
00:20:49,581 --> 00:20:51,583
All right, it's a gamble now.

479
00:20:54,628 --> 00:20:55,587
Submissions are now closed.

480
00:20:55,671 --> 00:20:57,673
- Please reveal your color chip.
- This isn't easy.

481
00:20:59,675 --> 00:21:00,842
We have two rainbows.

482
00:21:02,928 --> 00:21:04,471
Hold on.

483
00:21:05,889 --> 00:21:07,349
Please reveal your rock card.

484
00:21:07,432 --> 00:21:08,809
What did they choose?

485
00:21:13,355 --> 00:21:14,314
Do I go first?

486
00:21:14,398 --> 00:21:16,358
JAE JAE, would you like to place?

487
00:21:16,441 --> 00:21:17,276
Yes.

488
00:21:18,694 --> 00:21:20,946
- Please choose a color.
- Blue.

489
00:21:21,029 --> 00:21:22,656
You have placed five on blue.

490
00:21:22,739 --> 00:21:24,616
Stella Jang, would you like to place?

491
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:26,034
I'll go with red.

492
00:21:26,118 --> 00:21:27,619
You have placed one on red.

493
00:21:27,703 --> 00:21:29,913
Did someone choose the red stand?
No one did.

494
00:21:29,997 --> 00:21:31,790
- Maybe she's stacking it for later.
- She should've just placed it

495
00:21:31,873 --> 00:21:33,625
on one of the other two in this round.

496
00:21:33,709 --> 00:21:35,836
Why didn't you choose green?
It would've collapsed.

497
00:21:37,796 --> 00:21:40,299
<i>It was a matter</i>
<i>of the stacked penalty points</i>

498
00:21:40,382 --> 00:21:43,468
<i>going to either John or Jin-ho.</i>

499
00:21:44,177 --> 00:21:45,137
Stella.

